-- title:
--   Zero-component transport along the Vélu coordinate map
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a Weierstrass curve over $\mathbb{Z}$ with $\Delta_W\neq 0$, let $p$ be an odd prime, and let $Q$ be a point of $W$ base changed to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}=\mathrm{AlgebraicClosure}\ \mathbb{Q}$ of exact additive order $p$; write $S=$ `oddOrderSummingSet` $Q\ \lfloor p/2\rfloor$ for the finite set of coordinate pairs of the points $k\cdot Q$, $1\le k\le \lfloor p/2\rfloor$ (the coordinates of $0$ being recorded as $(0,0)$). Let $W'$ be a further integral Weierstrass curve and $u\in\overline{\mathbb{Q}}^{\times}$ such that $W'$ base changed to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is the image of the Vélu quotient `veluQuotient` of $\overline{W}$ by $S$ (same $a_1,a_2,a_3$, with $a_4$ replaced by $a_4-5\sum_S\mathrm{veluT}$ and $a_6$ by $a_6-b_2\sum_S\mathrm{veluT}-7\sum_S\mathrm{veluW}$) under the variable change $(u,0,0,0)$. Let $q$ be a prime with $q\mid\Delta_W$, $q\nmid c_4(W)$, $q\mid\Delta_{W'}$, $q\nmid c_4(W')$, let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $q$ a non-unit of $A$, and assume $A$-valuation of $u$ equals $1$. Finally let $(x,y)$ be a nonsingular affine point of $\overline{W}$, with the corresponding point not lying in the subgroup of integer multiples of $Q$, and let $h'$ witness that $\bigl(u^{-2}\,\mathrm{veluX}_S(x),\,u^{-3}\,\mathrm{veluY}_S(x,y)\bigr)$ is a nonsingular affine point of $\overline{W'}$. The conclusion is an equivalence: this image point satisfies `InZeroComponentAt` for $W'$ at $A$ — i.e. it is $0$, or its $x$-coordinate is outside $A$, or both coordinates lie in $A$ and their residues give a nonsingular point of the reduction of $W'$ over the residue field of $A$ — if and only if there exists $k$ in the subgroup generated by $Q$ with $(x,y)-k$ satisfying the same condition for $W$ at $A$.
--
--   This is the transport law for the identity components of the reductions at a prime of multiplicative type under a $p$-isogeny, stated for the explicit Vélu coordinate map rather than for an abstract homomorphism with the given kernel; classically it reflects the behaviour of component groups of Tate curves under isogeny. It is used by [`WeierstrassCurve.exists_quotientDatum_of_galois_stable_primeCard`](thm.html#WeierstrassCurve.exists_quotientDatum_of_galois_stable_primeCard) to produce the quotient datum attached to a Galois-stable subgroup of prime order.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_WeierstrassCurve_inZeroComponentAt_veluCoord_iff_of_multiplicative.lean

